"""P2-9 (a2, a3, a4, c4) -- unit/face_removal: one breaking rule along one line per
surface cell, on fixtures where the answer is known.

Fixture: ./input (generated by ./make_input.py) -- the Hoeser lab configuration made
uniform: T_gas 1866 K (T_flame_expr), h 700 W/m2K (h_expr), one flaw 8 um, no
Weibull, a 24 x 24 x 64 mm block, insulated (Neumann-0) sides, 20 s.

MODES
  --offline   a2: (i) source -- the column path and the line path call the ONE
              reconstruction / scan / remap; (ii) SHEET; (iii) COLD; (iv) DECOMP;
              (v) fr_multi / fr_id_remap on every leg run here; (vi) the area rule
              at every tilt (initial interior faces).
  --floor     a3 (+ c4's first half): T00 (key 1) at dx 2 / 1 / 0.5 mm (P2-28: key 0 retired).
  --tilt      a5 (+ c4's second half): the tilted planes at 1 mm (and 2 mm).
  --curved    a6: SPH and BORE at 1 and 2 mm (make_input.py's curved fixtures).
  --check     re-reduce existing outputs (no runs), every block.
P2-9 rev 2 renumbered the packet's rows: the old a2 block is a3 (i)-(v), the area
rule (vi) now reads the smoothed-fraction normal, and (vii)-(x) are new; the floor
is a4 and the tilts a5 (bar 4 %).
Every leg writes output/<leg>/{argv.sh, run.log, run*}; legs are serial, -np 4.

THE RATE. The surface's normal position = mean over INTERIOR lines (along the
plane's dominant axis, >= 4 cells from every side, and the surface >= 4 cells from
both ends of the line throughout the window) of (sum of solid fraction along the
line) x dx x mu_true; least squares over 5-20 s. Key 0 has no fraction field: its
column position is (k_top - klo + 1/2) dz + phi_top, the same quantity (phi is the
level set z_s - z_c).
"""
